168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (In a world increasingly dominated by superficial opinions and depthless perspectives, meaningful and thoughtful analysis is more important than ever. The Critical Lens was born out of the desire to encourage students from the University of Bologna to share their unique perspectives on the events shaping our international landscape. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The main aim of this project is to offer well-researched, nuanced and thoughtful essays and provide a platform for students to strengthen their academic writing skills and critical thinking outside the classroom. The United Nations Students Associations firmly believes that informed discussions begin with the sharing of different ideas, perspectives and reflections; in a time where we are encouraged to simplify narratives, this magazine aspires to challenge this dangerous assumption. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (In this inaugural volume, we invited students to engage and reflect on the theme of war. The essays we received tackled the topic from a variety of angles across different contexts. The essays selected for this volume stood out for their depth, originality and analytical cut. Alongside the essays, our editorial team worked on an additional report focused on the situation of humanitarian assistance in conflict-driven contexts to broaden the discussion.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
