<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (1. Russia, Belarus, and the War in Ukraine: The Most Obvious Case. The IOC suspended the Russian Olympic Committee in October 2023 for incorporating Ukrainian sports organizations from the occupied territories, violating the Olympic Charter; as a result, Russia cannot participate as a national delegation at the 2026 Games. Yet a limited number of Russian athletes have been admitted as Individual Neutral Athletes \(AIN\): a category introduced after the 2022 invasion of Ukraine and first applied at Paris 2024. AIN athletes compete without a flag, anthem, or national symbols and undergo strict vetting to ensure they have no ties to the military or have not publicly supported the invasion. This compromise remains controversial: for many international observers and sports professionals, neutrality does not erase the political meaning of Russian participation, it simply reshapes it.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
