353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (power and influence collapsed, leaving vertiginous power vacuums. Second, the response of the Clinton administration was to cut US military spending by 40%, with most of the cuts affecting oversea bases \(McFate, 2014\). This clearly implied that regions where control and stability depended from the brittle power equilibrium of the cold war suddenly saw the superpowers retreat. Most of these countries had an unstable, post colonial / cold war government incapable of structuring an effective administration or state defence. As with the noblemen in control of the Northern Italian provinces, 'The revenue enjoyed from the sale of strategic resources is also directed at creating parallel military budgets that then pay for alternative security structures supplied by the private sector.' \(Kinsey, 2006. p. 54\). As clearly observed in recent years with, for example, the Wagner group linked Midas Resources' licensed contract in 2020 with the Central African Republic's gold mine of Ndassima in exchange for security assistance to the central government. \(Philip Obaji Jr, 2024\).)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
