/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (2024 became the deadliest year on record for humanitarian personnel worldwide. During that year, 383 humanitarian workers were killed, another 308 were wounded and 125 have been kidnapped. The wave of violence continued unabated in the first half of 2025, with the number of incidents and victims already more than double the annual totals recorded in most years before 2021.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (Tom Fletcher, the new UN Under-Secretary-General for Humanitarian Affairs and Emergency Relief Coordinator, during an OCHA council, decried that aid workers are being killed at an unprecedented rate. He called on States to protect humanitarians, uphold international law and call time on this era of impunity. These numbers will send shockwaves around the humanitarian community especially on the front lines of the response. The vast majority of deaths are national staff working for the UN, non-governmental organizations, and the Red Cross movement.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
