/Title (Private Security Sector in the International Community. The international landscape has proven to be a breeding ground for the private security sector, and attempting to understand it implies treating it like a profitable business venture. Offering a strong answer to regional insecurity, the corporate soldiers are destined to grow in number and wealth in the near future. The public opinion on the matter is rather condemning, as well as concerned with the ethics, as already seen in the well-documented involvement of DynCorp \(American\) in prostitution rings in Bosnia in the 90s \(Bailes et al, 2007\). Scholars on the matter argue that 'There is plenty of evidence that private armies are more disciplined and)
